Ravi (CSM): Kicking off a thread for Skylift onboarding 5m ago they reported lots of 429s during initial roll to staging. Renewal check-in next Wed so flagged as high priority. They said it happens when users open multiple tabs at once.

Tess (Support Eng): Do we have logs / sample UA? 429 on init often = preflight/token pool exhaustion or preflight window hit.

Ravi (CSM): Customer provided this short log:```
2026-03-25T21:10:02Z WARN preflight deny tenant=skylift count=210 window=1s
2026-03-25T21:10:02Z ERROR http 429 preflight_quota_exceeded
2026-03-25T21:10:03Z INFO http /v1/session 200 user=skylift-web UA=Skylift/2.1.0
```

Ibrahim (DevEx): 210/s is a classic stampede. Are they using SDK auto-fetch in every micro-frontend or exchanging on server?

Ravi (CSM): They said each micro-frontend calls `RedwoodSDK.init()` on mount with default settings. Also there are cross-domain iframes that mount widgets independently.

Nora (Solutions Eng): Recommended steps: 1) Disable SDK auto token prefetch for embedded widgets. 2) Centralize token issuance: one backend endpoint returns session token per user and reuse across tabs. 3) If cross-origin frames, use postMessage to share token from parent.

Tess (Support Eng): Short-term mitigation: add randomized splay before init to spread traffic over 1-3s. Also add graceful retry on 429s. Snippet we gave them:```js
// splay before init
setTimeout(()=>RedwoodSDK.init(), Math.random()*1500 + 200);
// exponential retry for 429
let tries=0;
function initWithRetry(){
  tries++;
  RedwoodSDK.init().catch(err=>{
    if(err.status===429 && tries<6){
      const backoff = Math.min(2000, 100*Math.pow(2,tries)) + Math.random()*300;
      setTimeout(initWithRetry, backoff);
    }
  });
}
initWithRetry();
```

Ravi (CSM): They asked if we can change tenant quota while they test fixes. Renewal pressure 30.

Nora (Solutions Eng): We can approve a temporary bump. Propose increase preflight per-tenant from 200/s -> 800/s for 6 hours while they validate. Must coordinate with ops and monitor token service saturation.

ops-bot: CR-8077 opened: tenant=skylift preflight quota bump 200->800/s for 2026-03-25T22:00:00Z to 2026-03-26T04:00:00Z. Notifying #eng-oncall.

Ibrahim (DevEx): I'll add an onboarding doc blurb: "Avoid per-component token fetch; use single token per session. If using multiple frames, share tokens via postMessage to parent frame." Also adding a troubleshooting checkbox to the onboarding playbook.

Tess (Support Eng): After they validate, please post here with success/failure so we can close CR-8077. If errors persist, we can keep the bump or consider increasing tenant pool size.

Ravi (CSM): I'll update Skylift with steps and ETA for the patch. One customer asked whether SDK could expose a built-in splay option 50ms-2s default. Ibrahim, can you track that as a DevEx request?

Ibrahim (DevEx): Yep added to backlog: DX-1294 "SDK init splay option + single-token examples for multi-frame apps."

Ravi (CSM): Thanks team. I'll loop back after their staging test around 23:30 UTC. :thumbsup:
